  "notes": "CodePDE frames PDE solving as a code generation task: given a PDE description, an LLM produces an executable numerical solver whose nRMSE against ground-truth trajectories is used as the evaluation signal. The benchmark spans 5 PDE families (Advection, Burgers, Reaction-Diffusion, Compressible Navier-Stokes, Darcy Flow) with 100 instances each. Harbor treats each family as one task (aggregate nRMSE over the 100 instances) and assigns reward=1 if that aggregate is below 0.05, so num_tasks=5 and the Harbor-aligned pass rate is the average reward over the 5 tasks. The paper evaluates 16 LLMs; here we record results under CodePDE (Reasoning + Debugging + Refinement, best-of-12) together with two existing agentic workflows (FunSearch-PDE and AIDE-PDE) for a representative subset of models (Gemini 2.5 Pro, Claude-3.7-sonnet, DeepSeek-R1, GPT-4o, o3)."
}
